  "generated_text": "1. **Rewrite the quadratic equation:**\n   The equation $az^2 + bz + c = 0$ can be rewritten as $az^2 + bz = -c$.\n\n2. **Apply the triangle inequality:**\n   By the triangle inequality, $|az^2 + bz| = |-c| \\leq |az^2| + |bz|$.\n\n3. **Substitute the given conditions:**\n   Since $|a| = |b| = |c| > 0$, we have $|az^2| = |a||z|^2$ and $|bz| = |b||z|$. Thus, $|az^2| + |bz| = |a||z|^2 + |b||z|$.\n\n4. **Set up the inequality:**\n   Therefore, $|c| \\leq |a||z|^2 + |b||z|$.\n\n5. **Solve for $|z|$:**\n   This implies $|z| \\leq \\frac{|c|}{|a| + |b|}$.\n\nConclusion:\n   The final answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{|c|}{|a| + |b|}}$.",
